# Branch & PR Rules (mandatory for every agent, including Cursor cloud/background agents)

## PR base branch — read this before `gh pr create` or any "Create PR" action

**Always open pull requests against the integration branch, never against `main` or `live-*`.**

Resolve the PR base branch in this order:

1. `base_branch` in `climaybe.config.json`.
2. Otherwise `staging`, if it exists: `git ls-remote --exit-code --heads origin staging`.
3. Only if neither exists, stop and ask the human which base to use. Do **not** fall back to `main` silently.

Always pass the base explicitly — tools default to the repo's default branch (`main`):

```bash
gh pr create --draft --base staging   # or the base_branch from climaybe.config.json
```

Cloud/background agents: when the platform opens the PR for you, set the target/base branch to the resolved base. If a PR was opened against `main` by mistake, retarget it (`gh pr edit <n> --base staging`) instead of merging it.

## Hard rules

- Never open a PR whose base is `main` or `live-*`. `staging → main` release PRs and `staging-<alias> → live-<alias>` PRs are created by climaybe workflows, not by agents.
- Never push, commit, force-push, or rebase onto `main`, `live-*`, or `staging-<alias>` branches directly.
- Branch feature work off the resolved base branch (`git switch -c feat/... origin/staging`).
- Open PRs as **draft**; keep them draft until the Bugbot / code review has finished and is clean. Do not merge your own PR without human approval.
- Keep climaybe sync commit markers intact: `[hotfix-backport]`, `[stores-to-root]`, `[root-to-stores]`.
